Igor D. WonderLlama wrote:

> I agree with David here.  The point is not to make the easy game
> harder.  The point is to make the dificulty more consistent.

A simple way to accomplish this is to disallow the creation of powerful
wands on the lower levels. For example, don't create wands of wishing,
polymorph, and death on levels 1-5. Bones creation already works this way
(no bones for levels 1-3).

However, this would radically change the philosophy behind NetHack. In
NetHack, all items have the same generation chance per item class on all
dungeon levels (the distribution between the various item classes may
differ per dungeon branch).

Tweaking the generation chance on a per-level basis would turn NetHack
into Moria, where items are only created on an "appropriate" depth (but
sometimes not).

Let's not make all roguelikes the same.

